          "title": "Patruni e Sutta",
          "subtitle": "Social",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Patruni e Sutta is an Italian drinking card game from Calabria, Sicily, and the province of Taranto, usually played in teams."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Patruni e Sutta, meaning master and slave, is a social drinking game practiced with wine or beer in parts of southern Italy. It may use regional Italian, Sicilian, or French cards."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "4, 6, or 8 in two teams players use the table arrangement described for Patruni e Sutta."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Italian, Sicilian, or French cards"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Italian, Sicilian, or French cards, score area, and enough table space for play."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Deal to two teams according to the local pack and player count."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
